BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mammal Furs\, Brown County State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261031T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261031T140000
UID:fa7a284181d8ea1b732f3ba629c4fb0a@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Did you know that not all fur is the same? Different animals u
 se their fur for camoflauge\, protection\, and keeping warm in a variety o
 f habitats. Visit the Nature Center to learn about Indiana&#39\;s native m
 ammals. Learn about their habits\, habitats\, play a short game\, and touc
 h real animal furs!
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Nature Center\, 1405 S.R. 46 W\, Nashvi
 lle\, IN 
URL:https://on.in.gov/browncountysp
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Snake Meet and Greet\, Brown County State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261031T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261031T153000
UID:fe3c6a481e34aa29d141734e94f89597@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Come to the Nature Center for an up close and personal look at
  one of Indiana&#39\;s native snakes! Learn about their unique traits\, th
 e threats they face\, and how snakes affect your life! Participants may pe
 t the snake at the end of the program. Please be aware this program involv
 es a live animal.
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Nature Center\, 1405 S.R. 46 W\, Nashvi
 lle\, IN 
URL:https://on.in.gov/browncountysp
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Autumn Leaves Revisited\, Brown County State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261101T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261101T113000
UID:8865dd4540b8c2bc71eda5ce5ad77a15@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever wondered how and why our forests change into the
 ir beautiful fall colors? This program explains just that! Join a naturali
 st as we walk through how leaves transform through the seasons and why the
 y turn into the colors we see in the fall on the microscopic level! Stick 
 around after the program for a fun coloring activity to help you recognize
  and remember what changes our green leaves into yellows\, oranges\, reds\
 , and browns.
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Nature Center program room\, 1405 S.R. 
 46 W\, Nashville\, IN 
URL:on.in.gov/browncountysp
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Vintage Video\, Brown County State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261101T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261101T143000
UID:cc0824b0f6172b3f46adac89dc2b7f17@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Join a park naturalist and view a 1940s era advertisement for 
 Indiana State Parks! Learn about the mission of Indiana State Parks\, see 
 highlights of some of our famous locations\, and learn how as our understa
 nding of our resources changes\, so must our policies and practices! The p
 rogram and video lasts 30 minutes total.
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Nature Center\, 1405 S.R. 46 W\, Nashvi
 lle\, IN 
URL:https://on.in.gov/browncountysp
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fall Color Hike: Lake Strahl\, Brown County State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261102T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261102T114500
UID:a6d41155761318e54a07290518137d35@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Join a park naturalist for a guided hike of Trail 6 around Lak
 e Strahl! Hear about the history of the lake\, the surrounding Strahl Vall
 ey\, and learn about the animals that make it their home\, all while enjoy
 ing beautiful fall colors. The section of Trail 6 around Lake Strahl is co
 nsidered easy to moderate. It has some short staircases\, uneven surfaces\
 , tree roots\, and possible&nbsp\; wet spots. The trail is less than a mil
 e and will take about 45 minutes to complete. Meet at the Lake Strahl park
 ing lot.
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Lake Strahl parking lot\, 1405 S.R. 46 
 W\, Nashville\, IN 
URL:https://on.in.gov/BrownCountySP
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
