BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Full Moon Hike\, Brown County State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261223T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261223T200000
UID:42789a02de9884001fdb0e1d9dfb05dc@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Join a park naturalist for a guided night hike on the Salt Cre
 ek Trail! The Full Moon is the brightest night of the month\, leading to i
 nteresting views along the creek. Learn about December&#39\;s full moon th
 is year\, the Cold Moon. The Salt Creek Trail is rated very easy\, but sho
 uld be considered moderate in the dark. The trail has some minor slopes\, 
 a short stretch of lawn\, and possible wet or icy spots depending on weath
 er. Our route is&nbsp\; about 2 miles total and will take about an hour to
  complete. Please do not bring pets on night hikes. Red flashlights are pr
 eferred for night vision and can be loaned to hikers on request. Hike canc
 ellation policy : Hikes will be cancelled if there is lightning\, temperat
 ures below 0 degrees Farenheit\, temperature indexes above 105 degrees Far
 enheit\, or a wind advisory. If a hike is cancelled\, gatehouses will be i
 nformed. The phone number for the North Gatehouse is 812-988-5230.
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Olympic Pool parking lot\, 1405 S.R. 46
  W\, Nashville\, IN 
URL:https://on.in.gov/BrownCountySP
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
